cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Metriplectic Completion of the Frohmanian Symplectic Tether: Thermodynamic Structure and Lean Formalization for the Navier–Stokes Equations (Lean formalization, imported tether kernel, finite-dimensional viscous model, and companion paper)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin Stanley
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Texas, United States
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-metriplectic-ns"
keywords:
  - metriplectic
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Frohmanian Symplectic Tether
  - Lean 4
  - abstract algebra
  - Galerkin truncation
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization and working paper. Proves energy conservation and
  entropy production for abstract metriplectic systems; imports the
  Frohmanian tether kernel (frohmanian-tether-sdiff, commit 8b7bd67) and
  derives the damping obstruction, a tether-summand obstruction and a sign
  obstruction from it; and constructs a concrete finite-dimensional
  metriplectic system with viscous dissipation and a 3-mode triad instance
  with non-vacuity lemmas. Condition C2 for the tether kernel is not proved.
  The finite-dimensional model is not derived from Navier-Stokes, and the
  continuum Navier-Stokes(-Fourier) equations are not recovered or
  formalized. Not a Clay Millennium Problem proof; kernel checks are not
  PDE or physical proofs.
